From 166940092f5af8bc1d621beb24de5cf79c89ecd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangyicong <wangyicong@bytedance.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:17:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(sm90): update FP4 MegaMoE backends

Port internal optimization e77d501bf686e435eaba1994482109df8faf2478
onto the vLLM v0.32.0 DeepGEMM pin and its Torch operator interface.
Retain the final GPU fixture route-index correction from 09f5008a0.

Preserve the upstream SS padded-row/decode cost model, 8-token fine buckets,
ultra-sparse EP8 decode helpers, activation/reduction and vectorized scatter.
Preserve the optional RS kernel and byte/sign packer with fixed import-time
backend selection, explicit SS/RS calls, GS128/64 activation scales, GS32
weight scales, SiTU guards and per-call SM budgets. Keep V4.1 diagnostics.
RS/SS share activation workspaces but require separately packed raw weights.
Use flattened Torch schemas and the release native-library facade.

Original commit description: perf(sm90): update FP4 MegaMoE backends
Detailed optimization contracts are retained in docs/sm90-fp4-upstream-port.md.
Historical verification claims in that document refer to the original tree;
native compilation and GPU validation of this port are still required.

Co-authored-by: TRAE (GPT-6) <traecli@bytedance.com>
Signed-off-by: trae-solo-agent <solo-agent@trae.ai>
